    <moqui.device.DeviceConfig deviceConfigId="CFG_PROCESS_PID_TANK_LEVEL" configTypeEnumId="DctApplyConfig" purposeEnumId="DcpRunConfig" deviceTypeEnumId="DtMoquiPlcProcessPID" configName="Tank Level PID Startup Config" description="Full ProcessPid configRecipe surface plus the two supervisory alarm thresholds (folded into this same config since both are recipe values bound to TANK_LC; the thresholds are not literal ProcessPid FB inputs, just parameters carried on the same device for convenience). Tuned values confirmed by the developer: gain=10, integrationTime=60s, derivationTime=2s, setpoint=50%, outputMin/Max=0/100, levelLowLowThreshold=5%, levelHighHighThreshold=95%. atSetpointHysteresis=2% is an untuned starting value (status-only field, low risk) flagged for field tuning. deviationInversion=N because deviation=setpoint-feedback (not inverted) already gives the correct direct-acting sense: feedback below setpoint increases the output, opening the inlet valve. setpointFreezeEnable/ outputFreezeEnable start at N; both are overridden dynamically every scan by the Main FSM output function, so their static recipe value only applies before the very first scan." controlMethodEnumId="DcmPIDControl" />
